            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A right-angled triangle has an interior angle of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "45^{\\circ}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Is it always isosceles?",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Explain by using the tangent ratio.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. $\\tan45^{\\circ}=\\frac{O}{A}=1$, so $O=A$ and the triangle is isosceles.",
      "worked": "Let $O$ and $A$ be the opposite and adjacent sides relative to the $45^{\\circ}$ angle.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan45^{\\circ}&=\\frac{O}{A}\\\\\\frac{O}{A}&=1\\\\O&=A\\end{align*}$$\nThe two shorter sides are equal, so the triangle is always isosceles.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 29
  },
